@page "/"
@inject ProofingCatalog Catalog

<PageTitle>Identity CSP</PageTitle>

<h1>Identity CSP</h1>
<p class="muted">
    A Credential Service Provider that performs <strong>delegated identity proofing</strong>
    (NIST 800-63A rev4): a verified responsible adult vouches for a minor. The CSP is
    CSP-of-record and expresses assurance on the <strong>FAST IDIAL</strong> scale.
</p>

<FluentCard Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
    <h3>FAST IDIAL ladder</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>IDIAL 4</strong> — ≈ NIST IAL2 (e.g. Login.gov / commercial IAL2 CSP)</li>
        <li><strong>IDIAL 3</strong> — the practical middle ground most payers/providers operate at</li>
        <li><strong>IDIAL 2</strong> — ≈ NIST IAL1; the <em>minimum delegate floor</em> for issuing a minor credential</li>
        <li><strong>IDIAL 1 / below</strong> — too weak; not issuable</li>
    </ul>
</FluentCard>

<FluentCard Style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
    <h3>Proofing methods offered</h3>
    <table class="csp-methods">
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Yields</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var m in Catalog.Methods.Values)
            {
                <tr><td>@m.Label</td><td>@m.Idial</td></tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</FluentCard>

<FluentCard>
    <h3>Delegation rules</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Ceiling</strong> — the minor's effective assurance can never exceed the delegate's.</li>
        <li><strong>Discount</strong> — delegated proofing is a recognised-but-distinct pathway, marked "via delegation".</li>
        <li><strong>Floor</strong> — below IDIAL 2, no minor credential may be issued.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Run one on the <a href="proof">Proof</a> page; an issuer consults the resulting proofing event so the assurance basis travels in the credential.</p>
</FluentCard>

<style>
    .csp-methods { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.85rem; }
    .csp-methods th, .csp-methods td { text-align: left; padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.2); }
    .csp-methods th { font-size: 0.72rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; opacity: 0.75; }
</style>
